{% commandanatomy
   command="read"
   subcommand="summary"
   input="--dir raw_reads/"
   option="--output read_summary"
   optionSub="optional" /%}

`segul read summary` calculates summary statistics for raw sequence reads in FASTQ format. For assembled contigs, see [Genomic Contig Summary](/docs/cli-usage/contig-summary/).

{% aside type="note" %}
The `--phred`, `--dup-size`, and `--plot` options, the extra statistics, and the Complete mode duplication, overrepresented sequence, and adapter results are available in SEGUL v0.25.0 and later. Check the [Installation Guide](/docs/installation/update/#segul-cli) to update SEGUL.
{% /aside %}

## Input formats

- Gunzip Compressed FASTQ (.fq.gz/.fastq.gz), including BGZF
- Standard FASTQ (.fq/.fastq)

SEGUL detects the compression from the file content. Each file is read once and summarized on all CPU cores, and BGZF files are also decompressed in parallel.

## Usage

```bash
segul read summary -i raw_reads.fq.gz
```

or using directory input:

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir
```

The output file will be saved as `read-summary.csv` (along with the Complete mode archives and `report.json`) in the `Read-Summary` directory.

To specify the output directory, use the `--output` or `-o` argument:

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir -o read_dir_output
```

You can also use the `--prefix` argument to specify the prefix name of the output files:

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir -o read_dir_output --prefix my_read_summary
```

## Summary modes

SEGUL provides three modes to calculate summary statistics for raw reads:

- **Minimal**: read count only (`minimal-read-summary.csv`)
- **Basic**: per-file and per-read summary statistics in a single CSV (`read-summary.csv`)
- **Complete** (default): all Basic statistics plus per-position and relative-position profiles, read length × quality, distributions, duplication, overrepresented sequences, adapter content, paired-end consistency, cohort balance, and full statistics in `report.json` (`report.json` is also written for Minimal and Basic runs; see [Reproducibility, Replay & Reports](/docs/cli-usage/reproducibility/)).

Use the `--mode` option to choose `minimal`, `basic`, or `complete` (`default` is kept as an alias for `basic`):

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir --mode basic
```

## Statistics

Basic statistics for raw reads:

- Number of reads, empty reads, and bases
- Read length min, max, mean, median, SD, N50, N90, L50, and auN
- Base counts (A, C, G, T, N, other), GC/AT/N content, and strand skew (AT-skew, GC-skew)
- Per-read GC shape (SD, divergence from normal, peak count)
- Arithmetic mean, min, and max base quality, plus error-rate–aware effective mean quality and mean error rate
- Base shares at Q10, Q15, Q20, Q30, and Q40, plus distinct Phred quality count
- Per-read mean quality, low-quality reads (< Q20), expected errors per read and per 100 bp, expected error-free read share, reads with < 1 expected error, and read-level base survival at Q10, Q20, and Q30
- Sequence complexity (dinucleotide entropy) and low-complexity read share
- Homopolymer runs (≥ 6 bp), max run length, homopolymer vs non-homopolymer quality gap, and 3'-terminal poly-A/C/G/T tail shares
- Header metadata: sequencing platform hint, Illumina chastity-failed (`:Y:`) reads, and distinct run/lane group count
- Quality score offset (Phred+33 or Phred+64)

Complete mode adds:

- Quality quartiles, 10th and 90th percentiles, effective quality, read survival, and base composition at each read position (`read-pos-summary.zip`)
- Relative-position (0–100%) quality and base profiles, read length × quality bins, expected-error and complexity distributions, plus read length, quality, and GC distributions (`read-dist-summary.zip`)
- Summary positional scalars: 5'-to-3' quality drop, effective Q20/Q30 spans, and 5'-head composition bias span
- Automatic R1/R2 paired-end consistency (`pairs.csv`) and cohort-level pooling balance and robust outliers (`cohort-outliers.csv`)
- Duplication across every read of each file, with the number of copies of each sequence (see below)
- Overrepresented sequences, above 0.1% of all reads, with the adapter they match. Reads longer than 75 bp are compared by their first 50 bp
- Adapter content by position for Illumina Universal, Nextera, Illumina Small RNA, poly-A, and poly-G
- Technology- and library-aware QC checks (`--qc-profile auto|short-wgs|amplicon|long-ont|long-hifi`)
- All of the above in `report.json` (`<PREFIX>_report.json` with `--prefix`), which SEGUI opens as an interactive report. Open it in the terminal with [`segul view summary`](/docs/cli-usage/view-summary/)

## Comparison with other tools

Complete mode covers the core read quality checks of [FastQC](https://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/projects/fastqc/), [fastp](https://github.com/OpenGene/fastp), [NanoPlot](https://github.com/wdecoster/NanoPlot), and [SeqKit](https://bioinf.shenwei.me/seqkit/) in a single pass, while adding error-probability–aware quality metrics, sequence complexity and homopolymer diagnostics, paired-end sync checks, and cohort-level balance and outlier detection. fastp also trims and filters reads, which SEGUL does not.

| Feature | SEGUL | FastQC | fastp | NanoPlot | SeqKit (`stats`) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Read & base counts, GC content | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | Read/base counts | ✓ |
| Q10, Q15, Q20, Q30, Q40 base shares | ✓ (all 5 + read-level survival) | — | Q20, Q30 | Threshold counts | Q20, Q30 (`-a`) |
| Effective mean Q (error-rate) & expected errors | ✓ (per-base & per-read EE, error-free %) | — | — | Error-rate mean Q | — |
| Length metrics (N50, N90, L50, auN) | ✓ (all 4 + empty reads) | Min/max only | Mean only | N50 | N50 (`-a`) |
| Quality by position | Quartiles, mean, effective Q, read survival | Quartiles | Mean | — | — |
| Relative read-position profile (0–100%) | ✓ (quality & composition) | — | — | — | — |
| Read length × quality relationship | ✓ (length-stratified Q & EE) | — | — | ✓ | — |
| Base composition, strand skew, & 5'-head bias | ✓ (per-position, AT/GC skew, bias span) | Per-position only | Per-position only | — | — |
| GC distribution & anomaly quantification | ✓ (curve + normal divergence & peak count) | Curve only | — | — | — |
| Sequence complexity & homopolymer Q gap | ✓ (dinucleotide entropy, runs, 3' tails, Q gap) | — | Low-complexity / poly-X filter | — | — |
| Header metadata (platform, chastity `:Y:`, runs) | ✓ | — | — | — | — |
| Duplication | Every read, exact with `--dup-size 0` | First 100k distinct | Every read (hashed) | — | — |
| Overrepresented sequences | Every read | First 100k distinct | Sampled reads | — | — |
| Adapter content by position | ✓ | ✓ | Detected for trimming | — | — |
| Pass, warn, and fail checks | ✓ (technology/library QC profiles) | ✓ (fixed short-read) | — | — | — |
| R1/R2 pair sync & quality-drop check | ✓ (automatic across directory) | — | Single pair | — | — |
| Cohort pooling balance & robust outliers | ✓ (CV, Gini, P90/P10, dropouts, MAD outliers) | — (needs MultiQC) | — (needs MultiQC) | — | — |
| Per-tile quality, k-mer content | — | ✓ | k-mer counts | — | — |
| Insert size & read trimming/filtering | — | — | ✓ | — | — |
| Many samples in one report | ✓ | — | — | — | Table only |
| Charts & viewers | PNG/SVG/PDF; SEGUI & terminal viewers | HTML report | HTML report | HTML/PNG/SVG | — |

Use `--qc-profile` (`auto`, `short-wgs`, `amplicon`, `long-ont`, or `long-hifi`) to match pass, warn, and fail thresholds to your sequencing platform and library type.

## Duplication

SEGUL compares the full sequence of every read in the file. FastQC follows only the first 100,000 distinct sequences, which can misjudge long or sorted files.

Counting every distinct sequence exactly takes a lot of memory. By default, SEGUL keeps a uniform sample of 100,000 distinct sequences and counts their copies across all reads:

- The duplicate share is estimated with an error of about 0.3% of the distinct sequences.
- The levels chart uses the exact copy counts of the sample.
- Files with fewer distinct sequences are counted exactly.
- The sample uses about 30 bytes per sequence, about 3 MB per file by default.

Use `--dup-size` to change the sample size. Larger samples are more accurate, and `0` counts every distinct sequence exactly:

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir --mode complete --dup-size 1000000
```

Duplication results are the same with any number of threads. Overrepresented sequences are found among all reads. In files with many distinct sequences, their counts can be short by up to 0.025% of reads, listed as `max_error_pct` in `report.json`.

## Quality score offset

SEGUL detects the quality score offset from the first reads. Use `--phred 33` or `--phred 64` to set it.

## Charts

Add `--plot` to also write charts to `<OUTPUT>/plots`. Complete mode adds charts of quality by position (`pos-qscore-box_<sample>`), relative-position effective quality (`rel-pos-qscore`), read length (`length-dist`), quality by read length (`length-qscore_<sample>`), mean read quality (`read-qscore-dist`), expected errors per read (`expected-errors_<sample>`), sequence complexity (`complexity-dist`), GC content (`gc-dist_<sample>`), N content (`pos-n-content`), adapter content (`adapter-content_<sample>`), duplication (`duplication_<sample>`), and R1 vs R2 Q30 bases per pair (`pair-q30`):

```bash
segul read summary -d /raw_read_dir --mode complete --plot
```

## All options

| Option                 | Description                                                    |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-d`, `--dir`          | Directory with FASTQ files                                     |
| `-i`, `--input`        | FASTQ files. Allows wildcards                                  |
| `-f`, `--input-format` | Input format: `auto` (default), `fastq`, or `gzip`             |
| `--mode`               | Summary mode: `complete` (default), `basic`, or `minimal`      |
| `--phred`              | Quality score offset: `auto` (default), `33`, or `64`          |
| `--dup-size`           | Distinct sequences kept to estimate duplication. Default: `100000`. `0` counts all |
| `--qc-profile`         | QC check profile: `auto` (default), `short-wgs`, `amplicon`, `long-ont`, or `long-hifi` |
| `--plot`               | Also write charts to `<OUTPUT>/plots`                          |
| `-o`, `--output`       | Output directory. Default: `Read-Summary`                      |
| `--prefix`             | Prefix of the output files                                     |
| `--force`              | Overwrite an existing output directory                         |
| `--log`                | Log file path. Default: `segul.log`                            |
